# MEDIAINFO
Nixpkgs: mediainfo
Source: https://mediaarea.net/en/MediaInfo
Description: Unified display of the most relevant technical and tag data for video and audio files
Version: 24.06

## Commands

### Basics
- mediainfo [file]: display general information about a file
- mediainfo --Help: show help and available options

### Essentials
- mediainfo --Full [file]: show full information (all available tags)
- mediainfo --Output=HTML [file]: export information in HTML format
- mediainfo --Output=JSON [file]: export information in JSON format

### Intermediaries
- mediainfo --Info-Parameters: list all available parameters for custom output
- mediainfo --Language=raw [file]: show parameter names instead of labels

### Advanceds
- mediainfo --Inform="Video;%DisplayAspectRatio%" [file]: extract a specific parameter (e.g., aspect ratio)
- mediainfo --Inform="file://template.txt" [file]: use a custom template file for formatting

### Uncommons
- mediainfo --LogFile=[file].log [file]: write output to a log file

## Tips
- use --Output=JSON | jq for easy parsing in scripts
- custom templates are powerful for batch processing media libraries

## Disclaimers
- mediainfo only reads metadata; it does not modify the media files

## Alternatives
- ffprobe: part of ffmpeg, more focused on stream details for transcoding
- exiftool: better for images and document metadata

